    "english":  "The sweet-smelling vengai blossoms fall like drops of gold\nupon the dark boulders of the mountain slopes,\nwhere the hill-folk guard the ripening millet from flying parrots.\nThe swift tiger leaps through the bamboo thickets under the silent moon,\nyet through this perilous path of roaring streams and lurking beasts,\nthe lord of the mountain comes nightly to our secret tryst.\nMy heart trembles with dread at every gust of wind:\nif he truly loves me, why does he risk his precious life in the dark woods\ninstead of asking my kinsmen for my hand in an honorable wedding?",
